[[systemd: Service Management]]

* systemd Service management: starting, stopping, enabling, and checking services with systemctl, and understanding what “enabled” vs. “active” means.

systemctl status cron.service

Single-purpose checks, which are great in scripts because they set an exit code (0 = yes):

bash
systemctl is-active cron.service
systemctl is-enabled cron.service
systemctl is-failed cron.service